WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.122
The purpose of my program is a game where you click a

2
00:00:03.122 --> 00:00:05.360
moving ball on a target to get points.

3
00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:09.292
When the green flag is clicked, the reset block resets

4
00:00:09.292 --> 00:00:11.770
the program and sets my score to zero.

5
00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:15.444
My code works by using if blocks in this part to score

6
00:00:15.444 --> 00:00:18.529
my clicks. When I click the ball in the green area, I

7
00:00:18.529 --> 00:00:21.615
get fifty points. This is because the block here that

8
00:00:21.615 --> 00:00:24.060
checks if I'm touching green becomes true.

9
00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:28.050
Then the repeat block runs ten times. Each time, the

10
00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:30.910
glide block moves the ball to a random spot.

11
00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:36.669
When I click the ball in the yellow area, I get twenty

12
00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:39.764
five points. This is because the block here that checks

13
00:00:39.764 --> 00:00:41.790
if I'm touching yellow becomes true.

14
00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:47.686
And when I click the ball in the red area, I lose twenty

15
00:00:47.686 --> 00:00:51.138
five points. This is because the block here that checks

16
00:00:51.138 --> 00:00:53.210
if I'm touching red becomes true.

17
00:00:56.270 --> 00:00:59.575
And it also uses if else in this part to tell me how I

18
00:00:59.575 --> 00:01:02.697
did. My score ended up at fifty, which is more than

19
00:01:02.697 --> 00:01:04.350
zero, so it says good game.

20
00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.078
Last, the block here that checks if my score is over

21
00:01:08.078 --> 00:01:11.011
five hundred stays false. I only got fifty points, so

22
00:01:11.011 --> 00:01:12.560
the program doesn't say wow.

23
00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:16.283
If I were to change this if like this, for example

24
00:01:16.283 --> 00:01:19.339
changing the five hundred to a ten, the program would

25
00:01:19.339 --> 00:01:22.568
run differently. My fifty points would be more than ten,

26
00:01:22.568 --> 00:01:25.624
so at the end it would also say, wow, that's a lot of

27
00:01:25.624 --> 00:01:28.680
points. So the number in the if block really matters.

